<title>BELGIUM: EU farm experts fail to agree animal quotas.</title>
<headline>EU farm experts fail to agree animal quotas.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A special tariff quota for the import of animals from East European countries has been blocked in the European Union's special agriculture committee, an EU official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a brief discussion on Tuesday but no agreement could be reached. It will now go on the Irish Presidency's list for the December Farm Council,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The proposal to allow imports of Eastern European farm animals at a reduced tariff had run into difficulty because of the EU's GATT commitments.</p>
<p>&quot;Under the GATT agreement any relaxation of tariffs for Eastern Europe must be available to every GATT partner and this has brought out the protectionists,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
